Merger Agreement Excerpt:

“Primary Material Adverse Effect” means any event or circumstance that, whether considered individually or in aggregation, (i) has a material adverse impact on the Company’s financial condition, operations, or strategic direction, or (ii) would, by virtue of such impact, prevent, delay, or materially impair the Company’s ability to consummate the transactions contemplated by this Agreement. Notwithstanding any other provision herein, the exemptions set forth in this Section apply exclusively to events affecting the general operational and financial facets of the Company as described in (i), and expressly do not apply to any event or circumstance that directly impairs the Company’s ability to consummate the Merger. In particular, while fluctuations in economic indicators, worldwide shifts in capital markets, and uniformly applied industry-wide regulatory changes are excluded from triggering a Material Adverse Effect under clause (i), no such exclusion shall be available for any adverse condition that hinders or delays consummation of the Merger.
